  "claimId": "DTM",
  "example": false,
  "notes": [
    "The tolerance was registered in the protocol commit named under protocolRef before any reference grid was generated, and is unchanged.",
    "Scope is measured cells only. Interpolated (IDW fill) cells are not covered: rasterizeDtm does not fill.",
    "terra builds the grid from the extent and resolution and does its own point-to-cell assignment and median. The fixtures and the comparison harness are this project's own.",
    "160 cells that share an edge on which an input return lies exactly were left out of the terra leg, as the protocol fixed in advance: terra numbers rows from the top and its rule for a return on an interior edge differs. That is an edge convention, not a median question.",
    "The numbers are computed by tests/dtmMedianCrossCheck.test.ts."
  ],
